# =============================================================================
# black_glass_candle — ignore rules
#
# Order matters: secret rules first, then build noise, then local state.
# Verify any new rule against a REAL file with:
#     git check-ignore -v --no-index <path>
# (plain `git check-ignore` skips already-tracked paths and will report nothing)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0. private/ — safety net: personal state must never be committed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live data is not here. It lives outside the repository entirely, at
# ~/Library/Application Support/glass_candle_tv/private, because a launchd job
# cannot read anything under ~/Documents (macOS TCC) and the feed-refresh agent
# has to read it. See scripts/lib-common.sh for the measurement, and
# docs/operations.md §1 for the layout.
#
# This rule is the backstop. An old checkout, a copy made in a hurry, or a stray
# `mkdir private` must never become committable: one rule covers the whole
# subtree, so "is this safe to publish" is answered by one question — is it
# under private/ or not.
#
#     private/                 what it holds, wherever it lives
#     ├── env                  deployment config (passwords, tokens)
#     ├── apps/FreshRSS/       cloned code
#     │   └── data/            ← subscriptions, categories, feeds, read state
#     ├── apps/rss-bridge/
#     │   └── config/config.ini.php
#     ├── etc/                 generated RSS-Bridge router + bridge config
#     ├── run/                 runtime scratch (services use TCP ports, not sockets)
#     ├── logs/                service and refresh logs
#     └── backups/             snapshots from scripts/backup.sh
private/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SECRETS — must never be committed
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The master env file: FreshRSS API password, Instagram burner sessionid,
# GitHub PAT, Cloudflare tunnel token.
#
# NOTE: the live file is <data dir>/private/env, outside the repo — see the
# section above. This stays because a stale .env at the root would otherwise be
# committed silently.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Generic secret containers, in case values get exported during debugging.
secrets/
.secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.kdbx

# RSS-Bridge holds its instance token + bridge credentials in the file at its
# application root. The .example template IS committed; the live file is not.
**/config.ini.php
!**/config.ini.php.example

# The FreshRSS clone's data/ holds config.php + the SQLite DB, which contains the
# user table and the API password hash.
**/config.php
**/config-user.custom.php
**/users/*/config.php

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Backups — a dump contains the whole feed DB and every subscription
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
backups/
*.opml.bak
*.sqlite.bak
*.tar.gz
!docs/**/*.tar.gz

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Swift build products (menubar app)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.build/
build/
*.app/
.swiftpm/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Runtime state
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
.pids/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. macOS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Icon?
